      "content": "The argument that a strong benefit \"cushion\" can disincentivize work is often related to the concept of \"poverty trap\" or benefit cliff concerns. While some evidence suggests this, real-world data is more complex than a simple direct causation. It is more likely that the *design* of the benefit system, such as phase-out rates, is the true driver, rather than the absolute benefit level itself, in influencing labor force decisions.",
